Z||000000||bocefas||12-19-2001||09:06 PM||||About 4 months ago, I won an auction for an Aero Front Fascia from a guy in New Orleans, with the ebay ID "LongrifleK".  I sent him a money order for $200, which was the pricwe of the item ($150) and the shipping ($50).  After a month of run-arounds from him, I have no choice but to go through ebay's fraud policy to try to get my money back.  They request all sorts of information, all of which I send, and patiently WAIT...and WAIT...and WAIT.  Well yesterday they congratulate me on my fraud, yes indeed I was defrauded, and they are going to give me $125 for my trouble...HHHHMMMMMMM....seems that even though they acknowledge the fact I lost $200, they won't cover shipping since they don't make money on it, and they charge $25 for the "investigation"....what a fuc&ing ripoff!!!  Well on the bright side I was able to get a fascia from an honest forum member(thanks fleabitdog) and my car is back together, but the whole losing $75 thing just chaps my a$$.  Just a heads-up to the "safe" environment on ebay.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Springtyme||12-19-2001||09:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bocefas:<BR><B>Well on the bright side I was able to get a fascia from an honest forum member(thanks fleabitdog) and my car is back together, but the whole losing $75 thing just chaps my a$$.  Just a heads-up to the "safe" environment on ebay.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Fleabit dog is the best =) I got GT vents and the side marker light I needed from him. I'm waiting for a Celica wing from a guy on Ebay. I sent him my 32 bucks, he said he'd let me know how much shipping was after he sent it and I'd pay that seperate. Well, I still haven't heard anything and I've emailed him a ton. If I don't hear from him by the new year I'm gonna have to look into that. Damn... and I really wanted that wing too...<P>||||reg||8
Z||000002||frontal lobe||12-19-2001||10:09 PM||||I'm sorry that happened to you.  That criminal sucks.  At least you got SOME of the money from ebay, which is better than many places you can buy/sell on the internet.  I think e-bay does a decent job, at least, but then I didn't just get stolen from.||||reg||1
Z||000003||bocefas||12-20-2001||08:30 PM||||C'mon, there has to be someone else out there to help me whine about this...it's the Holiday season, no one likes to be alone, especially after getting screwed over!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||PAUL88GT||12-21-2001||12:09 AM||||Point me to safer place than e-bay to buy and sell on the web and I will use it.  At least there is some recourse if you get screwed.  So far I have had no problem with e-bay, but I sell more that I buy. I always get nervous working outside of e-bay, even when using the Mall section of this forum.||||reg||1
Z||000005||bocefas||12-21-2001||06:34 AM||||Ebay is only as "safe" as the user you're dealing with, that's my point.  In order to have an ebay account, you must provide them with a valid credit card number, and they tell you right up front that if there is a problem dealing with your account and you are determined to be the one at fault, YOUR CARD COULD BE CHARGED FOR THE AMOUNT OF THE TRANSACTION.  I guess this only applies if EBAY gets screwed, not the user.  It just bothers me, especially since it's been a couple of months now and "the check is in the mail" from ebay...hell that's the line the guy fed me about the front fascia!!!||||reg||1
